    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nWith ui2 + `cmdheight=0`, after opening a directory listing the process cwd silently resets to the directory where nvim was launched whenever an error float opens (any failed command, e.g. `:xxx`). `:pwd`, `:!cmd` and relative paths then point at the wrong directory.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```sh\ncd /tmp\nmkdir -p /tmp/some-dir && echo '{}' > /tmp/some-dir/serve-latest.json\nnvim --clean -n --cmd \"set cmdheight=0\" \\\n  -c \"e /tmp/some-dir/serve-latest.json\" -c \"lua require('vim._core.ui2').enable()\"\n```\n\n```vim\n\" inside nvim:\n-          \" open the dir listing\n:pwd       \" -> /tmp/some-dir      (correct)\n:xxx       \" E492 -> ui2 error float opens\n:pwd       \" -> /tmp                (BUG: should stay /tmp/some-dir)\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe error float should not change the cwd — `:pwd` stays `/tmp/some-dir`.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\n`v0.13.0-dev-1261+g7e53d3ba4d` (present since the `:bcd` feature; affects nightly)\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nN/A\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nLinux\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nkitty 0.48.1\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-kitty\n\n### Installation\n\nBuilt from repo (Debug), `master` @ `7e53d3ba4d`\n\n### Follow-up\n\nI have a working fix in the https://github.com/erdivartanovich/neovim/tree/fix/window-keep-cwd branch and I'm happy to submit a PR if you think it is relevant. @justinmk\n",
